{"step_index":170,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T20:27:58Z","content":"The backend for the **NEXUS** platform is complete and verified alongside the React/Vite frontend.\n\nA walkthrough of the implementation and test results is available in [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/brain/296415ce-8ed0-4b1c-b8ba-a547de0a4137/walkthrough.md).\n\n---\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\nbackend/\n├── app/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── main.py                     # App entrypoint, CORS for React (:5173), error handlers, SQLite init\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   ├── router.py               # Aggregates /api sub-routers\n│   │   ├── health.py               # GET /health\n│   │   ├── cases.py                # GET /api/cases, GET /api/cases/{case_id}, POST /api/cases\n│   │   ├── network.py              # GET /api/network/{case_id} (NetworkX analysis)\n│   │   ├── entities.py             # GET /api/entities, GET /api/entities/{entity_id}\n│   │   ├── insights.py             # GET /api/insights/{case_id}\n│   │   └── upload.py               # POST /api/upload (TXT, CSV, JSON only)\n│   ├── models/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   ├── base.py                 # SQLAlchemy 2.0 Base & TimestampMixin\n│   │   ├── case.py                 # Case SQLite table definition\n│   │   ├── entity.py               # Entity SQLite table definition\n│   │   └── evidence.py             # Evidence SQLite table definition\n│   ├── schemas/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   ├── common.py               # HealthResponse, ErrorDetail, APIResponseEnvelope\n│   │   ├── case.py                 # CaseCreate, CaseResponse, status & priority enums\n│   │   ├── entity.py               # EntityResponse, EntityType, RiskLevel, LocationData\n│   │   ├── network.py              # GraphNode, GraphEdge, NetworkGraphData, GraphMetrics\n│   │   ├── insight.py              # CrimePattern, \n<truncated 2654 bytes>\nicle plates (`UP14 AB 1234`), and INR amounts (`₹12,50,000`).\n   - Clean architectural boundary ready for future drop-in upgrades with **spaCy NER** and the **Google Gemini API**.\n\n4. **Upload Endpoint (`POST /api/upload`)**:\n   - Restricted strictly to **TXT, CSV, and JSON** files. Rejects unsupported formats (e.g., PDF/DOCX) with a descriptive `400 Bad Request`.\n   - Computes cryptographic SHA-256 digests and extracts indicators.\n\n5. **CORS & OpenAPI Documentation**:\n   - Pre-configured CORS middleware for `http://localhost:5173` and `http://localhost:3000`.\n   - Automatic interactive Swagger docs at `http://localhost:8000/docs` and ReDoc at `http://localhost:8000/redoc`.\n\n---\n\n### Automated Verification Results\n\nBoth test suites passed:\n* **`backend/tests/test_phase1.py`**:\n  - `GET /health` -> 200 OK\n  - `GET /api/cases` -> 200 OK\n  - `GET /api/cases/case-sih-01` -> 200 OK\n  - `GET /api/cases/invalid-id` -> 404 (Structured error format)\n  - `POST /api/cases` -> 201 Created\n  - `GET /api/network/case-sih-01` -> 200 OK (NetworkX metrics verified)\n  - `GET /api/entities/ent-1` -> 200 OK\n  - `GET /api/insights/case-sih-01` -> 200 OK (2 patterns, 3 alerts, 4 metrics)\n  - CORS header check for origin `:5173` -> 200 OK\n* **`backend/tests/test_upload.py`**:\n  - `POST /api/upload` (TXT with SHA-256 and entity extraction) -> 201 Created\n  - `POST /api/upload` (CSV vehicle log) -> 201 Created\n  - `POST /api/upload` (JSON bank extract) -> 201 Created\n  - `POST /api/upload` (PDF upload rejection) -> 400 Bad Request\n\n---\n\n### How to Run\n\nFrom PowerShell:\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\backend\n& \"..\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n- Swagger UI: [http://localhost:8000/docs](http://localhost:8000/docs)\n- Health Check: [http://localhost:8000/health](http://localhost:8000/health)\n\n*(Recommendation: Set `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch` as your active IDE workspace to view the frontend and backend side-by-side).*","truncated_fields":["content"]}
